
<%doc>

</%doc>


<& /page/page_title.mas, title=>"Genome: <i>Solanum pennellii</i>" &>

<br>
<p>
  <& /util/sentence.mas, text => __x('{link}{i}{species}{end_i}{end_link} is a wild tomato that is relatively distant from the domesticated {link2}{i}{species2}{end_i}{end_link2}.'), link => '<a href="/chado/organism.pl?organism_id=19">', end_link => '</a>', link2 => '<a href="/chado/organism.pl?organism_id=1">', end_link2 => '</a>', i => '<i>', end_i => '</i>' , species => 'Solanum pennellii' , species2 => 'Solanum lycopersicum' &>  <& /util/sentence.mas, text => __x('It was sequenced by a group of scientists at MPI Golm and the Univeristy of Aachen and collaborators, under the direction of {person} and {person2}.') , person => 'Alistair Fernie' , person2 => 'Bj&ouml;rn Usadel' &>
<br>
  <& /util/sentence.mas, text => __x('It has been widely used for the construction of {link}mapping populations{end_link} and {link2}inbred lines{end_link2}.'), link => '<a href="/cview/map.pl?map_id=9&show_offsets=1&show_ruler=1">', end_link => '</a>', link2 => '<a href="/cview/map.pl?map_id=il6&show_offsets=1&show_ruler=1">', end_link2 => '</a>' &>
</p>

<br>

<p>
  <strong><& /util/sentence.mas, text => __x('Please, cite {i}{species}{end_i} genome as:'), i => '<i>', end_i => '</i>' , species => 'Solanum pennellii' &></strong><br>
  Bolger, A., Scossa, F., Bolger, M. E., Lanz, C., Maumus, F., Tohge, T., ... & Fernie A.R. (2014). <a href="http://www.nature.com/ng/journal/v46/n9/full/ng.3046.html">The genome of the stress-tolerant wild tomato species Solanum pennellii.</a> Nature Genetics 46, 1034–1038
</p>

<br>
<p><strong><% __('Abstract') |h %></strong><br><& /util/sentence.mas, text => __x('{i}{species}{end_i} is a wild tomato species endemic to Andean regions in South America, where it has evolved to thrive in arid habitats.'), i => '<i>', end_i => '</i>' , species => 'Solanum pennellii' &> <& /util/sentence.mas, text => __x('Because of its extreme stress tolerance and unusual morphology, it is an important donor of germplasm for the cultivated tomato {i}{species2}{end_i}.'), i => '<i>', end_i => '</i>' , species2 => 'Solanum lycopersicum' &> <& /util/sentence.mas, text => __x('Introgression lines (ILs) in which large genomic regions of {i}{species2}{end_i} are replaced with the corresponding segments from {i}{species}{end_i} can show remarkably superior agronomic performance.'), i => '<i>', end_i => '</i>' , species2 => 'S. lycopersicum' , species => 'S. pennellii' &> Here we describe a high-quality genome assembly of the parents of the IL population. <& /util/sentence.mas, text => __x('By anchoring the {i}{species}{end_i} genome to the genetic map, we define candidate genes for stress tolerance and provide evidence that transposable elements had a role in the evolution of these traits.'), i => '<i>', end_i => '</i>' , species => 'S. pennellii' &> <& /util/sentence.mas, text => __x('Our work paves a path toward further tomato improvement and for deciphering the mechanisms underlying the myriad other agronomic traits that can be improved with {i}{species}{end_i} germplasm.'), i => '<i>', end_i => '</i>' , species => 'S. pennellii' &></p>

<br>
